 To add a sound: drop the file in `public/sounds/`, then `playSound('file.mp3')` (and optionally
 `preloadSound('file.mp3')` on mount).
 
+## Character voices
+
+The dialogue scenes (pre-test, portal arrival, return, post-test) are voiced:
+Mia and Max each have their own voice in every language. The tracks are
+pre-recorded MP3s in `public/voices/<locale>/`, made with Google Cloud
+Text-to-Speech (Gemini-TTS, falling back to Chirp 3 HD), so the published game
+needs no API key and makes no calls to Google.
+
+1. Put `GOOGLE_TTS_API_KEY=...` in `.env` (gitignored; never a `VITE_` variable).
+2. `npm run voices -- --dry-run` lists every line → `docs/voices/<locale>.csv`.
+3. `npm run voices` records what is missing and updates `src/game/voiceManifest.js`.
+4. Commit `public/voices/` and the manifest.
+
+After `npm run i18n:import` changes the copy, run `npm run voices` again: only
+the changed lines are recorded (`--prune` removes tracks nothing uses). Voices,
+model and acting direction are at the top of `scripts/generate-voices.mjs`;
+`settings.voice` turns voices off, and they follow the HUD mute button.
+
